  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Two-Phase Commit (2PC) is a protocol for distributed transactions. It ensures all participants commit or all abort."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Key Concepts"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "key-terms",
      "data": {
        "terms": [
          {
            "term": "2PC",
            "definition": "A protocol for atomic distributed transactions."
          },
          {
            "term": "Coordinator",
            "definition": "The service that manages the 2PC protocol."
          },
          {
            "term": "Prepare Phase",
            "definition": "Phase 1: ask all participants if they can commit."
          },
          {
            "term": "Commit Phase",
            "definition": "Phase 2: commit or abort based on responses."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "How 2PC Works"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Phases"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "data": {
        "headers": ["Phase", "Action", "State"],
        "rows": [
          ["Prepare", "Participants vote and lock", "Resources locked"],
          ["Commit", "All commit or all abort", "Atomic outcome"]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Pros"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": ["Atomic outcome (all or nothing)", "Strong consistency", "Well understood"]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Cons"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Blocks during failures (resources locked)",
          "Slow (two round trips)",
          "Coordinator is a single point of failure",
          "Does not scale well"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "When to Use"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "2PC is rarely used in microservices. Use it only when strong consistency is absolutely required and the performance and availability trade-offs are acceptable."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Architecture"
      }
    },
    {
